# The facet-runtime commit this checkout of Facet Hawkes Assistant is built and
# tested against. Facet owns exact solving and solver routing, and this
# repository imports it as a path dependency at ../facet-runtime, so an older
# runtime is not a slower system -- it is a missing symbol at import time.
#
# This file is the single source of truth. CI reads it, and
# tests/test_runtime_pin.py fails if any document quotes a different commit.
#
# Raise it in the same change that starts depending on something newer. This
# commit also owns labeled Cartesian points and exact slope from a line's two
# structurally identified points, bounded affine-coordinate steps, and shared
# exact parallel/perpendicular through-point construction, with no model call.
# It also selects ordinal equation rewrites over exact rationals and makes
# ambiguous or missing source selection a terminal refusal without reasoning.
# It independently normalizes two source equations for exact relationship
# classification and semantic choice matching, including axis-aligned lines.
# Boolean relationship surfaces reuse that classifier and evaluate a unique
# explicit prompt proposition before semantically matching Yes or No.
# It also returns finite relation domain/range as named exact rational sets,
# refusing ambiguous or unsupported relations without model calls.
# It also classifies finite relations as functions and returns a conditional
# No with two exact source pairs sharing x and differing in y.
# It also projects explicit linear graph geometry into named exact interval,
# singleton or all-real-numbers parts, with no model fallback.
# Stated linear function properties are exact over rationals and ambiguity
# is terminal: no reasoning fallback may replace an unreadable slope or value.
# Continuous affine relations route separately from finite sets, corroborate
# equations against graph points, and reuse typed named projections.
# Affine equations also return one typed slope/y-intercept composite, preserving
# exact rationals and refusing vertical or ambiguous relations.
# Linear function graph choices compare exact slope/intercept semantics from
# page-owned alternatives and refuse missing or duplicate matches terminally.
# The tip of that repository may be ahead of it, and that is fine -- the pin is
# a floor, and the test checks the sibling is not below it.
